        "raw": "<p>How does Death Caller interact with effects that destroy a target if they&#39;re brought below a certain HP threshold?</p><blockquote><p>Death-Caller</p><p>Title</p><p>After a target destroys a target without dealing damage to it, put this card under the surviving target, covering everything above this line:<br />--------------------------------------------------------<br />Whenever this target reduces another target to 3 or fewer HP, destroy that target.</p></blockquote><p>The effecrts I&#39;m thinking of are KNYFE&#39;s Flawless Execution, Fixer&#39;s Tyre Iron or the Sentinels&#39; Fling Into Darkness.</p><p>I can see a few ways of the power working.</p><p>1) If you&#39;ve ever done damage to that target, you can&#39;t gain it. Book-keeping nightmare and silly. Included for completeness.</p><p>2) You damaged them to get the destroy effect to activate, so doesn&#39;t count.</p><p>3) Flawless Execution and Tyre Iron work as the damage is a separate thing, but Fling Into Darkness wouldn&#39;t.</p><p>4) You did not directly destroy the target with damage, i.e. HP were not reduced to 0 or less, so they all count.</p><p>Personally, I think 4 is correct, with 2 being an alternative interpretation. 3 is possible but seems needlessly fiddly and restrictive and 1 is obviously silly.</p><p>Thoughts from the community?</p><p>As an aside, Captain Cosmic is ripe for this one with all his construct destruction effects. Or, indeed, almost anyone if you have Imbued Vitality out.</p>",
