        "id": 131548,
        "name": "Nataraja",
        "username": "Nataraja",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/7feea3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-15T12:49:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Fling into Darkness works exactly like Tyre Iron and Flawless Execution do. The damage and destruction are separate events in all these cases.</p><p>All three are good for getting that title. In this game nothing happens simultaneously and everything that happens is its own discrete event. So you Fling a target, bring it to 4 HP or less, this triggers the rider on FiD and the target is destroyed without taking damage.</p><p>Now the real question is: who among the Sentinels gets the title? I'd say a Sentinel of your choice by rules, beause there's no indication the Writhe character did the destruction (other than fluff)</p><p>Another instance of poor wording: all cards that destroy a target say \"[you] destroy a target\". There's no indication that it's a target doing the destruction. Of course rule of common sense helps...</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:06:52.947Z",
